  "acrm---why-emergent-table": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><style>\n  .cmp--emg-first thead th.col-brand-head { background: #ebebeb; }\n  .cmp--emg-first tbody tr:nth-child(odd) td.col-brand { background: #f2f2f2; }\n  .cmp--emg-first tbody tr:nth-child(even) td.col-brand { background: #e6e6e6; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"cmp cmp--emg-first\">\n  <table>\n    <colgroup>\n      <col class=\"col-feature\" />\n      <col class=\"col-brand\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n    </colgroup>\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th class=\"col-feature\" scope=\"col\"><span class=\"visually-hidden\"></span></th>\n        <th class=\"col-brand-head\" scope=\"col\">\n          <img class=\"brand-logo\" src=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6a0edf12ef1a8562ed56d806/6a0ef94db7f0a045fab57060_logo.svg\" alt=\"Emergent\" />\n        </th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Jotform</th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Google Forms</th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Typeform</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">How you build</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">Describe it in plain English</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Templates, editor, AI generator</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Manual, field by field</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Templates, editor, AI assist</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Where responses live</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">A database table you own, plus any integration</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Jotform account</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Google Sheets</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Typeform account</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Response limits</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">No response caps</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Monthly submission caps by plan; the form stops at the cap</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">No limit</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Monthly response caps by plan; the form closes at the cap</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Code ownership</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">Full code export to GitHub on paid plans</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div></div>",
  "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { annualRecordCheck: \"Build an employee information form for my freight company's 140 employees. Every January, send each person their own record with last year's answers filled in, and let them confirm it or edit any field. Show me a dashboard of who has confirmed, who edited and who has not replied. Ten days after the send, email a reminder to everyone still open.\", legalNameChanges: \"Let my employees request a legal name change from their record. Ask for the new name and whether their Social Security card already shows it. If it does not, keep the old name in payroll until they show HR the updated card. Once HR marks the card as shown, send our payroll lead a direct message with the old and new name, and keep the old name in the record's history.\", missingFields: \"I am importing 86 staff records from an old spreadsheet for my dental group. Check every record for a blank home address or personal phone. For each person with a gap, send a link that asks only for the missing fields, not the whole form. Show HR how many gaps are filled and how many are still open, and let me remind the rest.\", managerDirectory: \"Give each store manager a directory of their own team with names, job titles and work phones. Keep date of birth, home address and Social Security number in a view only HR can open. If a manager needs a home address, let them send a request to HR with a reason, and log who asked, when and whether HR shared it.\" };</p>",
  "awb---how-to-step-2-des": "Group the questions under personal details, contact details, job details and emergency contacts. One section per screen keeps the form short on a phone, and HR can later resend a single section when only that part needs an update.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Staff Record Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"An employee information form is the record an employer keeps on each person: legal name, contact details, job title, start date, and emergency contacts. HR collects it at hiring and goes back to it whenever payroll or a manager needs a detail.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an employee information form online?\", \"a\": \"List the fields payroll and HR use, decide who may see each one, then put a database behind the form. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> creates the form, the employee record and the yearly confirmation from one description.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do I need on an employee information form to put someone on payroll?\", \"a\": \"Payroll needs the person's legal name and Social Security number as shown on their card, a home address and a signed Form W-4. Employers also complete Form I-9, and many collect bank details through a direct deposit form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to fill out an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Write your legal name exactly as it reads on your Social Security card, then a current home address and a phone you answer. Most versions also ask for an emergency contact and end with your signature and the date. If a field is unclear, ask HR before guessing, since payroll copies these answers as written.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an employee information form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A typical employee information form template fits on one page, grouped by section, with a signature line at the bottom. Paper suits a small team. Past a few dozen people, keeping every copy current becomes the hard part.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I customize an employee information form template for my company?\", \"a\": \"Cut every field nobody reads, then add the ones HR and payroll use, such as department and work location. Move private details like date of birth into their own section so fewer people handle them. A static employee information form PDF makes each of these changes slow, because every edit means a new file and every answer still gets retyped into payroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Several template sites let you download a free employee information form. Emergent is free to start as well, and its free tier covers building and publishing an online version that saves each answer to a record you can update.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should have access to an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Only the people whose work depends on a given field. HR and payroll need the full record, while a manager rarely needs more than work contact details. Keep Social Security numbers and bank details behind the tightest access, and store any paper copies in a locked file.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a basic new employee information form?\", \"a\": \"A basic version asks for legal name, address, phone, personal email, date of birth, job title, start date and one emergency contact. Tax and work eligibility forms travel with it in a new employee form packet.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should an employee information form be updated?\", \"a\": \"Once a year at minimum, when each employee checks their own record, and again whenever an address or phone number changes. Supervisors who need emergency contacts on site can keep a separate emergency contact form at the front desk.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
